      "message": "Can we mark the whole test as @ConnectivityModuleTest? It primarily/only tests code in the tethering module, and that\u0027s what @ConnectivityModuleTest is for, right?\n\nIf we can\u0027t mark the whole test as @ConnectivityModuleTest, then... not sure how we can separate the test into two without duplicating much of its code. I guess we could refactor/rename this method and have something like:\n\n    private void doTestUidsAllowedOnRestrictedNetworks(boolean shouldTestTApis) {\n        ... existing code...\n\n        if (shouldTestTApis) {\n            // Uid is in allowed list. Try file network request again.\n            requestNetwork(restrictedRequest, restrictedNetworkCb);\n            ...\n        }\n        ...\n    }\n\n    @AppModeFull(reason \u003d \"WRITE_SECURE_SETTINGS permission can\u0027t be granted to instant apps\")\n    @Test\n    public void testAllowedUidsCanUseRestrictedNetworks() throws Exception {\n        doTestUidsAllowedOnRestrictedNetworks(false);\n    }\n\n    @AppModeFull(reason \u003d \"WRITE_SECURE_SETTINGS permission can\u0027t be granted to instant apps\")\n    @Test\n    @ConnectivityModuleTest\n    public void testAllowedUidsCanRequestAndUseRestrictedNetworks() throws Exception {\n        assumeTrue(shouldTestTApis());\n        doTestUidsAllowedOnRestrictedNetworks(true);\n    }\n\nNot great, but better than lots of code duplication. I\u0027d prefer marking the whole test @ConnectivityModuleTest if that works.",
